========================================================
                 Crystal Eye Simulation Software
========================================================

~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Changes made by Ritabrata

18/01/2024

--------------------------------------------------------
Implementation of an environmental set up file (ce-setup.sh).
Sets up environmental variables:

CRYSTALEYE_SYS -> installation dir of the simulation software, the executables in
bin and lib are added to the system PATH and LD_LIBRARY_PATH for global access; 

CRYSTALEYE_DATA -> the CAD stl files and other data files (geometry gdml, volume 
position information, background spectral information) are installed in the data 
dir and used through this environment variable in the software;

CRYSTALEYE_MACRO -> the macro files required to run the simulation are installed in 
the macro dir and accessed through this environment variable;

--------------------------------------------------------
Addition of data dir to contain the CAD stl files for the geometry. Also may 
contain other hard coded data required for the simulation in future.

--------------------------------------------------------
Addition of doc dir for future use for storing documentation (doxygen) files.

--------------------------------------------------------
Modification of the main CMakeLists.txt file to remove CADMesh variables and
addition of the subdirectories.

TODO: Need to change the make file redistribution of the software structure.

--------------------------------------------------------
The sofware distribution have been modified to segregate and accommodate the 
functionalities like: geometry, Monte Carlo simulation, digitization, analysis,
eventviewer, etc. in diffrent folders in include and src subfolders.

geometry: Contains the detector structure (and SD declaration) for the MC simulation.

montecarlo: Contains all the simulation functionalities and generates the simulated 
data in a root data file. The main function (CESimu) to perform the simulation 
(have been moved) in the src/montecarlo folder.

analysis: Contains the functionalities for reading and analyzing the simulated data.
The main function CEAna calls for the analysis.

digitization: folder contains the digitization functionalities of the simulated data.

eventviewer: event viewing utilities.
  
--------------------------------------------------------

~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
28/02/2024

--------------------------------------------------------
The data dir is added with the gdml file containing the the geometry information
of the detector. It also have other files with the position information of 
different volumes.

Spectral data for different particle background at the LEO is added for the use 
of analysis purpose.  

--------------------------------------------------------
Modifications in the geometry implementation:

The location of the stl files are retrieved (in the detector construction class) 
from the system variable defined in the configuration file.

The CADMesh dependancy is removed by using an additional class to read and use the 
stl data. Consequently the procedure of reading and using the stl data in the 
detectorconstruction class has been modified.
 
--------------------------------------------------------
Modifications in the MC simulation:

The simulation functionalities have been optimized for the multithread run.

The main function (in CESimu.cc) can be run by providing different arguments
(CESimu -h for help).

The analysis class of the simulation is modified to rearrange and addition to 
the output data. Data tree are filled with the use of the container struct through 
the datamanager classes.

--------------------------------------------------------
Addition of analysis functionalities of the simulation data:

New classes added for the analysis of the simulated data. The main function 
in CEAna.cc calls for the analysis (CEAna -h for help). Different classes for the 
analysis of primary, calorimeter and anticoincidence data. Data I/O managed 
through the streamer class and analysis is managed through the AnalysisAction 
class.
  
--------------------------------------------------------
EventViewer implementation:

A graphical interface for viewing individual events from the simulation (data) 
has been implemented through EventViewer class and main function in CEView.cc
(CEView -h for help).

--------------------------------------------------------
